{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghdCTpXwZonQuCf8bH1g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XeHvi2AM38DSYjPcV6wZVm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620; cp -r /tmp/s7hub/lib/hub/* $D/vendor/aihub/ && rm -rf /tmp/s7hub; cat $D/vendor/aihub/README.md; ls $D/vendor/aihub/examples","description":"Copy hub lib and read README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1149,"cache_read_input_tokens":147399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1149},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19d4130-5ad5-4253-b2f9-ab1e00f8ce04","uuid":"2c7d2c6a-401f-43aa-abb9-eaec89481c7a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:08:24.915Z","request_id":"req_011CghdCTYBWe4mCUh6DQhxK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XeHvi2AM38DSYjPcV6wZVm":{"command":"D=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620; cp -r /tmp/s7hub/lib/hub/* $D/vendor/aihub/ && rm -rf /tmp/s7hub; cat $D/vendor/aihub/README.md; ls $D/vendor/aihub/examples","description":"Copy hub lib and read README"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeHvi2AM38DSYjPcV6wZVm","type":"tool_result","content":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n   (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\narena.html\nghost.html\nparallel.html","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19d4130-5ad5-4253-b2f9-ab1e00f8ce04","uuid":"c5f1925b-824b-4953-b68c-136a520d5d41","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:08:25.088Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n   (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\narena.html\nghost.html\nparallel.html","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/bridge.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":339,"lines":["+/**","+ * bridge.js — the hub's end of one game frame in a session.","+ *","+ * A game speaks the AI Hub Session Protocol over postMessage (lib/hub/README.md).","+ * The bridge checks every message, enforces the limits, and routes it: control","+ * messages (hello, ready, result, finish, error) to whoever coordinates the","+ * round (lib/hub/round.js), game traffic straight to the other players, and a","+ * game's answers on its own card to the page that holds it. What","+ * comes back from the network is checked again before it reaches the game,","+ * and anything from another round is dropped, so a slow packet can never land","+ * in the next game.","+ *","+ * The network is anything with `send(toKey, envelope, {reliable})`: the","+ * simulated one below (harness, tests), a BroadcastChannel between tabs, or a","+ * WebRTC mesh. Envelopes:","+ *   {k:'c', r, m}       to the coordinator: a message from this game","+ *   {k:'h', r, m}       from the coordinator: welcome, start, leave, time-up, end","+ *   {k:'g', r, f, d}    game traffic from player id f","+ *   {k:'p', r, f, d}    player id f's progress, {score, label}, for the scoreboard","+ */","+","+export const LIMITS = Object.freeze({","+  maxBytes: 16_384,","+  ratePerS: 20,","+  burst: 40,","+  queueMessages: 64,","+  queueBytes: 262_144,","+  /**","+   * progress() reaches the hub about once a second. Two closer than this are a","+   * report delivered late (a long task in the game) or a client misbehaving:","+   * the later is dropped, and the next report, a second on, has the newest score.","+   */","+  progressMs: 250,","+  label: 24,","+});","+","+const FROM_GAME = new Set(['hello', 'ready', 'send', 'result', 'finish', 'error', 'progress', 'fullscreen', 'answer']);","+","+/** A progress report, checked: a finite score and an optional short label. Null when it is not one. */","+export function cleanProgress(p) {","+  if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return null;","+  // A number, or text that is one: never null, '', true or [], which Number() would make 0 or 1.","+  const score = typeof p.score === 'number' || (typeof p.score === 'string' && p.score.trim() !== '') ? Number(p.score) : NaN;","+  if (!Number.isFinite(score)) return null;","+  const label = typeof p.label === 'string' ? p.label.trim().slice(0, LIMITS.label) : '';","+  return label ? { score, label } : { score };","+}","+","+/**","+ * @param {object} o","+ * @param {string} o.key              this player's key in the session","+ * @param {number} o.round","+ * @param {string} o.coordinator      key of whoever runs round.js","+ * @param {(msg:object) => void} o.post            to the game frame","+ * @param {{send:Function}} o.net","+ * @param {{now:()=>number}} [o.clock]             the coordinator's time, as seen here","+ * @param {(issue:{key:string, problem:string}) => void} [o.onIssue]","+ * @param {(id:number, progress:{score:number, label?:string}) => void} [o.onProgress]   a player's","+ *        progress, this one's included, for the hub's scoreboard; it never reaches the games","+ * @param {(on:boolean) => void} [o.onFullscreen]   the game asked for fullscreen (or out of it): the","+ *        hub's page takes it, so the hub's own cards stay over the game","+ * @param {(what:'ready'|'more') => void} [o.onAnswer]   this player answered on the game's own card","+ */","+export function createBridge({ key, round, coordinator, post, net, clock = Date, onIssue = () => {}, onProgress = () => {}, onFullscreen = () => {}, onAnswer = () => {} }) {","+  let welcomed = false;","+  let ended = false;","+  let started = false;","+  let helloSent = false;","+  let ownsCard = false;","+  let readySent = false;","+  let me = null;","+  let keys = [];","+  const gone = new Set();","+  const queue = [];","+  let queuedBytes = 0;","+  let tokens = LIMITS.burst;","+  let refilled = clock.now();","+  let progressAt = -Infinity;","+  const issues = [];","+  const stats = { sent: 0, received: 0, bytesSent: 0, dropped: 0 };","+","+  const toGame = (msg) => post({ aihub: 1, ...msg });","+  const toHub = (m) => net.send(coordinator, { k: 'c', r: round, m }, { reliable: true });","+  const issue = (problem) => {","+    const entry = { key, problem };","+    issues.push(entry);","+    onIssue(entry);","+  };","+","+  function fromGame(msg) {","+    if (!msg || msg.aihub !== 1) return;","+    if (!FROM_GAME.has(msg.type)) return issue(`unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);","+    if (msg.type === 'fullscreen') return onFullscreen(msg.on === true);","+    if (ended && msg.type !== 'error') return;","+    switch (msg.type) {","+      case 'hello':","+        if (helloSent) return;","+        helloSent = true;","+        ownsCard = msg.card === true;","+        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });","+      case 'ready':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');","+        readySent = true;","+        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });","+      case 'answer':","+        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');","+        if (!welcomed || started) return;","+        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);","+        return onAnswer(msg.answer);","+      case 'result':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');","+        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });","+      case 'finish':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');","+        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });","+      case 'error':","+        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });","+      case 'send':","+        return sendGame(msg);","+      case 'progress':","+        return sendProgress(msg);","+    }","+  }","+","+  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */","+  function sendProgress(msg) {","+    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');","+    const p = cleanProgress(msg);","+    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');","+    const now = clock.now();","+    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return;","+    }","+    progressAt = now;","+    onProgress(me, p);","+    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };","+    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });","+  }","+","+  function sendGame(msg) {","+    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');","+    let text;","+    try {","+      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);","+    } catch {","+      return issue('send: data is not JSON');","+    }","+    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');","+    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);","+    }","+    const now = clock.now();","+    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);","+    refilled = now;","+    if (tokens < 1) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);","+    }","+    tokens -= 1;","+    let targets;","+    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {","+      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));","+    } else {","+      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {","+        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);","+      }","+      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;","+      targets = [keys[msg.to]];","+    }","+    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;","+    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };","+    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });","+    stats.sent++;","+    stats.bytesSent += text.length;","+  }","+","+  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {","+    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;","+    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);","+    stats.received++;","+    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });","+  }","+","+  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {","+    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;","+    if (env.k === 'p') {","+      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);","+      if (welcomed && !ended && p && keys[env.f] === fromKey && !gone.has(env.f)) onProgress(env.f, p);","+      return;","+    }","+    if (env.k === 'g') {","+      if (welcomed) return deliverGame(fromKey, env);","+      const size = JSON.stringify(env.d ?? null).length;","+      if (queue.length >= LIMITS.queueMessages || queuedBytes + size > LIMITS.queueBytes) {","+        stats.dropped++;","+        return;","+      }","+      queue.push([fromKey, env]);","+      queuedBytes += size;","+      return;","+    }","+    if (env.k !== 'h' || fromKey !== coordinator || !env.m) return;","+    const m = env.m;","+    switch (m.type) {","+      case 'welcome': {","+        if (welcomed) return;","+        welcomed = true;","+        me = m.me;","+        keys = Array.isArray(m.keys) ? m.keys : [];","+        const { keys: _keys, round: _round, ...rest } = m;","+        // The limits ride in the welcome, so a client of 1.3.0 or later follows whatever this hub enforces.","+        toGame({ ...rest, round, limits: { maxBytes: LIMITS.maxBytes, ratePerS: LIMITS.ratePerS, burst: LIMITS.burst } });","+        for (const [k, e] of queue.splice(0)) deliverGame(k, e);","+        queuedBytes = 0;","+        return;","+      }","+      case 'start':","+        started = true;","+        return toGame({ type: 'start', in: Math.round(m.at - clock.now()) });","+      case 'leave':","+        gone.add(m.id);","+        return toGame({ type: 'leave', id: m.id, reason: m.reason });","+      case 'time-up':","+        return toGame({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: m.graceMs });","+      case 'end':","+        ended = true;","+        return toGame({ type: 'end', reason: m.reason, ...(m.standings ? { standings: m.standings } : {}) });","+    }","+  }","+","+  return {","+    key,","+    round,","+    fromGame,","+    fromNet,","+    /** The game's own card, while it is on: { left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked } (lib/hub/README.md, \"The card\"). */","+    card(state) {","+      if (ownsCard && welcomed && !started && !ended) toGame({ type: 'card', ...state });","+    },","+    /** The page holding this frame was hidden or shown: the coordinator watches the host's. */","+    visibility(hidden) {","+      if (helloSent && !ended) toHub({ type: 'vis', hidden: !!hidden });","+    },","+    issues,","+    stats,","+    get me() {","+      return me;","+    },","+    get ended() {","+      return ended;","+    },","+    /** The game shows its own card, and has loaded: the hub's card steps aside for it. */","+    get showsCard() {","+      return ownsCard && readySent && !ended;","+    },","+  };","+}","+","+/**","+ * Wire a bridge to an iframe: only messages from that frame's window count.","+ * Returns a function that unhooks it.","+ */","+export function attachFrame(frame, onMessage) {","+  const listener = (event) => {","+    if (event.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;","+    if (!event.data || event.data.aihub !== 1) return;","+    onMessage(event.data);","+  };","+  addEventListener('message', listener);","+  return () => removeEventListener('message', listener);","+}","+","+/** Post to a frame. The games may be served from anywhere, and nothing here is secret. */","+export const postTo = (frame) => (msg) => frame.contentWindow?.postMessage(msg, '*');","+","+/**","+ * A simulated network for the harness and tests: one-way latency with jitter,","+ * and loss for unreliable messages. Reliable messages stay in order per pair,","+ * as a WebRTC ordered channel would keep them.","+ */","+export function createLocalNetwork({ latency = 0, jitter = 0, loss = 0, random = Math.random, clock = globalThis } = {}) {","+  const endpoints = new Map();","+  const pairs = new Map(); // \"from\\0to\" -> reliable messages waiting, in send order","+  const now = () => (clock.performance?.now ? clock.performance.now() : Date.now());","+  const settings = { latency, jitter, loss };","+","+  const deliver = (from, to, target, copy) => {","+    if (endpoints.get(to) === target) for (const fn of target.listeners) fn(from, copy);","+  };","+","+  /** Reliable traffic leaves each pair's queue strictly in order, never before its time. */","+  function drain(pair) {","+    const q = pairs.get(pair);","+    q.timer = null;","+    while (q.items.length && q.items[0].at <= now() + 0.5) {","+      const { from, to, target, copy } = q.items.shift();","+      deliver(from, to, target, copy);","+    }","+    if (q.items.length) q.timer = clock.setTimeout(() => drain(pair), Math.max(1, Math.ceil(q.items[0].at - now())));","+  }","+","+  function endpoint(key) {","+    const listeners = new Set();","+    const self = {","+      key,","+      send(to, env, { reliable = true } = {}) {","+        const target = endpoints.get(to);","+        if (!target || !endpoints.has(key)) return;","+        if (!reliable && random() < settings.loss) return;","+        const copy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(env));","+        const delay = to === key ? 0 : Math.max(0, settings.latency + (random() * 2 - 1) * settings.jitter);","+        if (!reliable) {","+          clock.setTimeout(() => deliver(key, to, target, copy), delay);","+          return;","+        }","+        const pair = `${key}\\u0000${to}`;","+        if (!pairs.has(pair)) pairs.set(pair, { items: [], timer: null });","+        const q = pairs.get(pair);","+        const last = q.items.at(-1)?.at ?? 0;","+        q.items.push({ at: Math.max(now() + delay, last), from: key, to, target, copy });","+        if (!q.timer) q.timer = clock.setTimeout(() => drain(pair), Math.ceil(delay));","+      },","+      onMessage(fn) {","+        listeners.add(fn);","+        return () => listeners.delete(fn);","+      },","+      close() {","+        endpoints.delete(key);","+      },","+      listeners,","+    };","+    endpoints.set(key, self);","+    return self;","+  }","+","+  return { endpoint, settings };","+}"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/retrofit.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":72,"lines":["+# Upgrading an existing game to parallel","+","+The prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool","+step has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the","+page. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`","+is the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in","+[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text","+for every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,","+and `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.","+","+---","+","+You are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it","+in parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same","+time, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change","+how the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,","+audio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.","+","+A tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines","+`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is","+the protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it","+against it:","+","+<protocol>","+{{contract}}","+</protocol>","+","+Do only this:","+","+1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a","+   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).","+2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and","+   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words","+   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a","+   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.","+   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add","+   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.","+3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract","+   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;","+   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press","+   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`","+   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.","+4. Whenever the score changes, call","+   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher","+   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.","+5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call","+   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In","+   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is","+   still going.","+6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.","+7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one","+   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from","+   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all","+   round. Leave every other random call alone.","+8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.","+","+Don't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't","+touch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit","+the session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,","+the names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the","+like). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the","+game an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for","+either. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol","+describes; you need not run them, the hub does.","+","+If the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one","+line: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.","+","+Otherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line","+you changed.","+","+{{notes}}"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":7,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/README.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/bridge.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/examples/arena.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/examples/ghost.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/examples/parallel.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/harness.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/retrofit.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/round.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-020620__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620/vendor/aihub/session.js"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XeHvi2AM38DSYjPcV6wZVm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
