g? About 12: the walker teleporting along an edge, unwinnable boss fights, a cold open that waited 50 minutes, stuck states the player could not leave, and statues that could never be rescued.',\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran? The honest bot playthrough of the whole demo headless (about 6 seconds of real time for 13 minutes of game time): it found every softlock and balance wall in order.',\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran? The first version of the content validator: it passed while a spawn sat inside a wall, because it checked the wrong tile.'\n  ]],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    'What did you like most about the engine? The split between a deterministic fixed-step 2D engine and a 3D world drawn under it: the whole game runs headless in Node, and the rigs, the cel filter and the pen made a look quickly.',\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes: the pen and world.shape heights, per-tile stairs (each tile rises its full height), and which materials exist (no brass) took a few guesses. The pixel font lacks umlauts, accents, the em dash and the PlayStation symbols.',\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The rail system: the walker, junctions, quick turns, ski physics, lifts and jumps, with an automatic camera director that places fixed Killer7-style shots where a clear line to the hero exists.',\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine? Keeping two worlds of truth apart: the sim keeps its own geometry (a grid built from the same rows, or the same terrain function) because the 3D world is browser-only.',\n    'What did you change in the engine, and why? Six S7 PATCHes in my-3d2dge.js: new hats (beanie, ushanka, felt, beret, hard hat, race helmet, pillbox); face accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, shades, cigar, visor); gun-like held weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, camera, launcher); PlayStation button symbols by default; game.pauseBlock() so the AI Hub\\'s Create + Options never pauses; and font glyphs for Ä Ö Ü ä ö ü ß È É è é à — and ·. The 3D module is unchanged.',\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? A headless stand-in for World3D (geometry, rays and projection without three.js), so a 3D game\\'s rules and its picture could share one source of truth in tests.'\n  ]],\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\n    'What did you like most about this prompt? It is concrete about the deliverables and the process (one test command, headless tools, the shared machine) while leaving the design open, and the plan gave a full design to build to.',\n    'What was confusing? The plan names a different model and date in its file names; TASK.md\\'s names win, which STAGE.md says, but it is easy to miss.',\n    'What was the hardest thing to do? Scope: the plan describes nine areas, three bosses and every system at full depth; building all of it whole in one session meant writing the content compactly and leaning on automatic camera placement.',\n    'What would you change in this prompt? Say how long the demo should take a first-time player, and whether a bot finishing it honestly is the proof of \"complete\", so the effort can be aimed.'\n  ]],\n  ['CREDITS', [\n    'SKILLER7 — Seven Killers, One Mountain. Version ' + S7.VERSION + '.',\n    'Design, code, music, sound, voices and words: written for this demo by Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5), from PLAN.md.',\n    'Made with my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module (MIT) · three.js r182 (MIT) · Rapier 0.19.3 (Apache-2.0) · AI Hub session client 1.4.0 · Asset store entries converted from the Kenney Holiday Kit (CC0).',\n    'Inspired by Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005). An original game; no affiliation.'\n  ]]\n];\nS7.CREDITS = ['#SKILLER7', 'SEVEN KILLERS, ONE MOUNTAIN', '', '#THE SEVEN', 'Ansel Holle — The Sweep', 'Dagny Holle — Schuss', 'Ignaz Holle — Telemark', 'Rurik Holle — Mogul', 'Kasimir Holle — Yodel', 'Mireille Holle — Snapshot', 'Brigid Holle — Avalanche', '',\n  '#ROOM 7', 'Oma Holle', 'Sister Rosalind', 'The Concierge (Ambrose)', '', '#ON THE MOUNTAIN', 'Pim the Lift Boy', 'Murmel', 'Bellcaptain Augustin Grau', 'Die Lustigen Vier', 'Hansi Pulver, the Powder King', 'Mister Föhn', '',\n  '#MADE WITH', 'my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module (MIT)', 'three.js r182 (MIT)', 'Rapier 0.19.3 (Apache-2.0)', 'AI Hub session client 1.4.0', 'Kenney Holiday Kit (CC0)', '',\n  '#WRITTEN BY', 'Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5)', 'from PLAN.md', '', 'Inspired by Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005).', 'An original game; no affiliation.', '', '#THE SNOW WILL CONTINUE.'];\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XonYaE4AHNCQ8vjsYskjbm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
