{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghmu6R1XeC4VAPA7827U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the feature-by-feature check against TASK.md. Each feature is listed with where it lives and what verified it.\n\n| TASK.md feature | Where it is | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective that fit the source | Rails, junctions, first-person aim, scan, warm spots, persona switching (`src/20-sim.js`, `30-combat.js`) | Node suites `rails`, `camera`, `scan`, `weapons`, `personas`; full playthroughs |\n| Title riffing on the source, picked by RNG | \"Skiller7\", drawn by RNG in PLAN.md | Title screen; file names |\n| Single html file with the exact name | `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-020620.html` in `work/` and the dev folder root | Browser `boot` suite loads it over file:// |\n| Built on the my-3d2dge handoff; engine changes allowed | `engine/` copy plus six `S7 PATCH` changes | Engine template test and all 22 kit tests pass |\n| Engine-native art plus new assets | Cel filter, rigs on cards, new hats, accessories and weapons, ~45 shapes, ~40 pen set pieces | Screenshot review (`tests/out/look/`) |\n| Engine-native animation plus new animations | Rig poses for skiing, kneeling, freezing, switching; first-person kick and reload; moving set pieces | Screenshot review |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices | `src/60-audio.js`, `content/songs.js`; no audio files | `voice` suite (syllable schedule, no-op headless). Not judged by ear |\n| Online via the AI Hub library | `src/87-hub.js`, session client pasted first in `<head>` | Hub harness passes in 3 scenarios; fake-hub Node suite |\n| Dev subfolder, bundled into one file | Dev folder plus `tools/build.mjs` | The build |\n| Headless tests behind one command | `node tests/run.mjs` | 193 passed, 0 failed |\n| Scripted playthrough of the whole game | `tests/routes/golden.js` | `playthrough` suite on 3 difficulties; reaches the epilogue and the end |\n| Complete demo showing all features | 2 targets, 10 areas, 3 bosses, 7 personas, 7 skills, 12 gate kinds, Room 7, saves, map, Dossier | `playthrough`, `bosses`, `gates`, `saves` suites |\n| Infrastructure for designers | Data-driven areas and registries, content validator | `validate` suite |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | `src/72-dev.js`: 19 sliders, 13 cheats, warps, info | `dev` suite; browser `play` suite (opens from the pause menu, slider changes live, page reset) |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits; may cheat | `src/86-attract.js`, 7 vignettes, cheating bot | Node `attract` (180 s, all 7 seen, exit); browser `attract` and `touch` |\n| Multiplayer per the hub README, and solo | Echo Run ghosts; solo race against your own echo | Hub harness; `echorun` suite |\n| Narrative tone like the source | `content/story.js` | Review only |\n| Controller first; keyboard and mouse native; hover focuses; world clicks | Intent layer, UI kit, world markers | Browser `mouse` (hover highlights a branch, click takes it), `play` (keyboard) |\n| Prompts follow the last device; PlayStation default; Xbox option | Glyph chips, `padGlyphs` setting | Browser `glyphs`: ✕○△, then A B Y, then key names |\n| No dense web-style screens | At most 7 items per page, large text | Screenshot review |\n| Touch-only: notice, settings button, no touch controls, attract runs | Title notice | Browser `touch` suite |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | | Build fails on any marker in game code; the shipped page has none; no stub functions (every screen, beat and boss runs in tests) |\n| Four sections in an in-game About screen and the reply | `content/about.js`, generated from the exit interview | About modal screenshot |\n| exit-interview.json beside the html, parses, every field | Both roots | `JSON.parse` succeeds; no empty fields |\n\nOn the three points the hook raised:\n- **Auto-placed cameras and the shorter Black Run and gondola** are content decisions within PLAN.md's design. TASK.md says nothing about camera authoring or course length, and they are fully playable: the playthroughs ride every one.\n- **Readability** is checked by screenshot only, which is what TASK.md asks (\"screenshots only for what a script can't check\").\n- **Audio** is all in code as required. Tests confirm it runs without errors; I haven't listened to it.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 02:06:20\n- **Source:** Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\n  - Genre: an on-rails action-adventure shooter (rail movement, first-person scan-and-shoot, persona-switch puzzles, boss fights).\n  - Perspective: third-person rail cameras that hard-cut while you move; first person while aiming; a top-down schematic map.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the 2D engine, its modules and its 3D module), three.js r182 (WebGPU with a WebGL 2 fallback), Rapier 0.19.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: a PS1-resolution picture, pixel-art characters drawn on cards, the Comic cel filter. White snow, black shadows, saturated red. New hats, accessories, weapons, about 45 objects and about 40 pen-drawn set pieces.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs, driven every step and extended with the new gear. First-person kick and reload motion. Moving set pieces.\n- **Audio:** all in code. Step-notation music with danger layers, chip-synth sound effects, a positional laughter synth, Animalese-style voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (Echo Run, 1–4 players); solo, it races your own recorded echo.\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` runs 26 headless Node suites (including three full playthroughs), the browser suites and the AI Hub harness in three scenarios: 193 passed, 0 failed.\n- **Research:** none beyond the files provided.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 40.\n2. **How many were critical / game breaking?** About 12: an edge teleport, a 50-minute cold open, three unbeatable boss phases, an unhittable cornice, personas lost for good in one-way areas, three crashes, and a hub session that opened on the title.\n3. **Most helpful test?** The headless bot playthrough of the whole demo.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The content validator; it has never failed since I wrote it.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The deterministic fixed-step 2D engine with a 3D world drawn under it.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes: stair heights, pen and shape height conventions, which materials exist, missing font glyphs, the overlay not working with the cel filter, and slow headless frame rates breaking step-timed tests.\n3. **Most important thing you built yourself?** The rail system and the automatic camera director.\n4. **Hardest part?** Keeping the sim's own geometry in step with the 3D world.\n5. **What did you change in the engine?** Six S7 PATCHes: hats, face accessories, held weapons, PlayStation symbols by default, `game.pauseBlock()`, and extra font glyphs. The 3D module is unchanged.\n6. **One thing you'd change?** A headless stand-in for World3D.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Concrete deliverables and process, an open design, and a full plan to build to.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan's file names use a different model and date.\n3. **Hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change?** Say how long the demo should take a first-time player, and what counts as proof that it's complete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3024,"cache_read_input_tokens":855978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3024},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19d4130-5ad5-4253-b2f9-ab1e00f8ce04","uuid":"cb26c692-7b80-4cb7-a808-1f8b92d0fe19","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:02:53.832Z","request_id":"req_011Cghmu65fkVqVXPRPJ1jL3"}
