 danger layers, chip-synth sound effects, a positional laughter synth, Animalese-style voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (Echo Run, 1–4 players); solo, it races your own recorded echo.\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs`: 27 Node suites (including the TASK.md feature suite and three full playthroughs), browser suites (including audio and readability), and the AI Hub harness in three scenarios: 229 passed, 0 failed.\n- **Research:** none beyond the files provided.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 40, plus one found by the TASK.md suite (speakers without portraits).\n2. **How many were critical / game breaking?** About 12: an edge teleport, a 50-minute cold open, three unbeatable boss phases, an unhittable cornice, personas lost for good in one-way areas, three crashes, and a hub session that opened on the title.\n3. **Most helpful test?** The headless bot playthrough of the whole demo.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The content validator; it never failed after I wrote it.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The deterministic fixed-step 2D engine with a 3D world drawn under it.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes: stair heights, pen and shape height conventions, which materials exist, missing font glyphs, the overlay not working with the cel filter, and slow headless frame rates breaking step-timed tests.\n3. **Most important thing you built yourself?** The rail system and the automatic camera director.\n4. **Hardest part?** Keeping the sim's own geometry in step with the 3D world.\n5. **What did you change in the engine?** Six S7 PATCHes: hats, face accessories, held weapons, PlayStation symbols by default, `game.pauseBlock()`, and extra font glyphs. The 3D module is unchanged.\n6. **One thing you'd change?** A headless stand-in for World3D.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Concrete deliverables and process, an open design, and a full plan to build to.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan's file names use a different model and date.\n3. **Hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change?** Say how long the demo should take a first-time player, and what counts as proof that it's complete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1971,"cache_read_input_tokens":880319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1971},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19d4130-5ad5-4253-b2f9-ab1e00f8ce04","uuid":"0896e476-ab16-44e7-9393-2a194eec3442","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:10:31.070Z","request_id":"req_011CghnVgFft5fQCtdHzah4m"}
