{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghoDWbueqcccCJVNLxSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook asks for a per-feature behavioural check against TASK.md. Here it is: each TASK.md requirement and the test that exercises its behaviour. The run stands at 232 passed, 0 failed, and nothing has changed since.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Behavioural test |\n|---|---|\n| Genre, perspective, core loop | `rails` (walk, junction, quick turn, ski, hockey stop, jump, lift), `camera` (shot frames the hero, hard cuts, aim reaches the eye), `scan`, `weapons`, `whiteouts`, `combat` |\n| Complete demo with all mechanics | Three playthroughs (cold open to credits), `personas`, `death`/rescue, `economy`, `gates` (each kind: right persona opens, wrong is refused, survives save/load), `npcs`, `saves`, `bosses` (each phase beaten), `story` (skipping a scene equals watching it) |\n| Dev mode, live sliders, reset | `dev` (every slider applies, walk speed moves the walker, reset restores defaults, god mode); browser `play` (opens from the pause menu, slider changes live, page reset, Escape closes) |\n| Attract mode | Node: starts after 10 s idle, plays all 7 vignettes, loops, any input returns to the title, cheats restored. Browser: real key and touch-tap exits |\n| Multiplayer | AI Hub harness passes 2-player, 4-player lossy and host-leave; fake-hub flow (connect, ready, countdown, send, progress, one result, leave, end); `echorun` |\n| Controller first, native keyboard and mouse | Browser `play` (keyboard walks), `mouse` (hover highlights a branch, click takes it), `glyphs` (DualSense ✕○△, then Xbox A B Y, then keys) |\n| Touch-only devices | Browser `touch`: notice shown, no touch controls, attract runs, a tap returns to the notice |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices | Browser `audio`: music, effects, laughter and voice measured audible on the output; no audio files; `voice` (deterministic syllables) |\n| 10-foot readability | Browser `readability` (text size against screen height) plus screenshot review, as TASK.md allows |\n| Art and animation | `boot` (picture drawn), `taskmd` (every pose runs, all weapon animations, assets present), authored-camera visibility check |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | Build-time scan plus `taskmd` |\n| Single file, exit interview, About | `boot`, `taskmd` |\n\nThe single HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in both `work/` and the dev folder root. The JSON parses and every field is answered.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 02:06:20\n- **Source:** Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\n  - Genre: an on-rails action-adventure shooter (rail movement, first-person scan-and-shoot, persona-switch puzzles, boss fights).\n  - Perspective: third-person rail cameras that hard-cut while you move, using hand-authored shots on set pieces and automatic shots elsewhere; first person while aiming; a top-down schematic map.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine, modules, 3D module), three.js r182 (WebGPU with a WebGL 2 fallback), Rapier 0.19.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: PS1-resolution picture, pixel-art rigs on cards, Comic cel filter. White snow, black shadows, saturated red. New hats, accessories, weapons, about 45 objects and about 40 pen-drawn set pieces.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs driven each step and extended with the new gear; first-person kick and reload motion; moving set pieces.\n- **Audio:** all in code: step-notation music with danger layers, chip-synth sound effects, a positional laughter synth, Animalese-style voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (Echo Run, 1–4 players); solo, it races your own recorded echo.\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs`: 27 Node suites (including the TASK.md feature suite and three full playthroughs), browser suites (including audio and readability), and the AI Hub harness in three scenarios: 232 passed, 0 failed.\n- **Research:** none beyond the files provided.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 40, plus a speaker without a portrait and six authored camera shots blocked by walls, all fixed.\n2. **How many were critical / game breaking?** About 12: an edge teleport, a 50-minute cold open, three unbeatable boss phases, an unhittable cornice, personas lost for good in one-way areas, three crashes, and a hub session that opened on the title.\n3. **Most helpful test?** The headless bot playthrough of the whole demo.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The content validator; it never failed after I wrote it.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The deterministic fixed-step 2D engine with a 3D world drawn under it.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - stair heights;\n   - pen and shape height conventions;\n   - which materials exist;\n   - missing font glyphs;\n   - the first-person overlay doesn't work with the cel filter;\n   - slow headless frame rates broke step-timed tests.\n3. **Most important thing you built yourself?** The rail system, and a camera director that plays the authored shots on set pieces and places fixed shots automatically everywhere else.\n4. **Hardest part?** Keeping the sim's own geometry in step with the 3D world.\n5. **What did you change in the engine?** Six S7 PATCHes: hats, face accessories, held weapons, PlayStation symbols by default, `game.pauseBlock()`, and extra font glyphs. The 3D module is unchanged.\n6. **One thing you'd change?** A headless stand-in for World3D.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Concrete deliverables and process, an open design, and a full plan to build to.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan's file names use a different model and date.\n3. **Hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change?** Say how long the demo should take a first-time player, and what counts as proof that it's complete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2077,"cache_read_input_tokens":900884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2077},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19d4130-5ad5-4253-b2f9-ab1e00f8ce04","uuid":"9be3cdb6-ee6d-4e40-a2e5-6afcfd389072","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:20:02.376Z","request_id":"req_011CghoDWFKyXv1Gbxrk5Qjh"}
